	spec: "/logout is the opposite of /login: /logout <id...> removes provider accounts from secrets/auth.ason by the ids /status shows, the provider's letter and the account's position in auth.all (a1 Anthropic, o2 OpenAI, g1 OpenCode Go); bare /logout asks for one account in a choice form. Completion offers the ids with account names. The /status Slot column and INSPECT subscriptions show these ids (with * on the session's account) instead of i/n, and so do the terminal and web status rows (Sub o3, shown when the provider has several subscriptions; Plan.account holds the id). Other entries (other providers, serper) stay untouched; removed positions renumber the rest, so sessions' chosen and /account-picked accounts of that provider are forgotten. Unknown ids and accounts from environment variables are refused with nothing written; the provider is not told. The web-login command formerly named /logout (task 3za) is /revoke <client id|all>, named by /clients; the browser's own 'Log out this browser' POST /logout stays.",
